title One Child Diagnosis - Target / Pending implementation
participant "Parent" as Parent
participant "Host" as Host
participant "Session" as Store
participant "Child Runtime" as Child
Parent -> Host : Invoke validated and permitted Agent call
Host -> Store : Atomically admit child and parent-call link
Store --> Host : Fixed child Session and execution
Host -> Child : Start once after commit
Child -> Store : Append own messages and tool results
Child -->> Parent : Permitted high-level progress
alt Child completes
  Child -> Store : Commit final message and terminal
  Store --> Child : Committed
  Child --> Host : Final summary
  Host -> Store : Commit parent Agent tool result
  Store --> Host : Committed
  Host --> Parent : Return summary
else Parent requests stop
  Parent -> Host : Stop original child execution
  Host -> Child : Propagate cancellation
  Child -> Store : Persist actual outcome when known
  Child --> Host : Actual outcome or unresolved state
  Host --> Parent : No fabricated success / no replay
end
note over Parent,Store
  Independent histories; parent retains summary only.
  An unresolved child keeps its execution occupancy.
end note
