title One Business Tool Call - Target / Pending implementation
participant "Model" as Model
participant "ToolPipeline" as Pipeline
participant "Host" as Host
participant "Mate" as Mate
participant "Session" as Session
Model -> Pipeline : Tool call
Pipeline -> Pipeline : Resolve trusted target and validate arguments
Pipeline -> Session : Commit call identity before confirmation or execution
Session --> Pipeline : Committed call
alt Invalid arguments
  Pipeline -> Session : Commit real error with safe public projection
  Session --> Pipeline : Committed
  Pipeline --> Model : isError=true; field errors and trusted definition
else Valid arguments
  Pipeline -> Host : Check permission / obtain required confirmation
  Host --> Pipeline : Decision for same prepared snapshot
  alt Allowed
    Pipeline -> Mate : Execute prepared business call
    Mate --> Pipeline : Result or business failure
    Pipeline -> Pipeline : Apply after hooks; fix final outcome
  else Denied
    Pipeline -> Pipeline : Fix denied error; no business request
  end
  Pipeline -> Session : Commit outcome and optional Skill count atomically
  Session --> Pipeline : Committed outcome
  Pipeline --> Model : Return final result
end
note over Pipeline,Session
  Commit failure stops further advancement and requires reconciliation.
  Never replay the business call to repair missing history.
end note
@enduml
